    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Are failed Apex resets tax-deductible?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Same as eval fees — typically yes as ordinary business expense if you have a serious trading business. Document each one for your records."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I file Apex income on Schedule C?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes for US traders. Apex payouts go on Schedule C as gross receipts, and you deduct trading-related expenses (eval fees, platform fees, data fees, automation tools, VPS, education) on the same Schedule C. Self-employment tax is calculated on Schedule SE based on net Schedule C income."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I owe self-employment tax on Apex payouts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes — 15.3% on the first ~$68,600 in 2026 (verify SSA wage base for the current year), then 2.9% on amounts above. This is on top of ordinary income tax, which can push the total tax rate to 35-50%+. Set aside 30-35% of every payout for tax obligations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What countries are restricted from Apex?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Roughly 84 restricted countries as of April 2026. The list includes OFAC-sanctioned countries (Iran, North Korea, Syria, Cuba, Russia, Belarus) plus some FATF gray-list countries and regions where KYC infrastructure is unreliable. Verify your country at support.apextraderfunding.com before purchasing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade Apex if I'm originally from a restricted country but live in the US?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Generally yes if you have legal US residency and US-issued KYC documents (driver's license, SSN, US address). Country of birth doesn't disqualify you — current residency and KYC documents do."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Apex have a mobile app?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex itself doesn't have a branded mobile app, but Tradovate (Apex's primary platform) has full iOS and Android apps. You can monitor your Apex account, place orders, and manage positions from the Tradovate mobile app."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade Apex on iPhone / Android?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes via Tradovate's mobile app. Order entry, charts, P&L, drawdown level all visible on mobile. Mobile is fine for monitoring and emergency exits but most traders run their primary desktop setup for active trading."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Apex vs Topstep — which is better in 2026?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex 4.0 has more flexible rules (50% consistency vs Topstep's stricter rules, 5-day between-payout minimum vs Topstep's similar requirement, allows news trading), more platform options (Tradovate / Rithmic / NinjaTrader / WealthCharts vs Topstep's TopstepX + ProjectX exclusive stack — ProjectX went Topstep-only in February 2026), and one-time fees vs Topstep's monthly. Topstep has the OG reputation and slightly tighter integration. For automation specifically, Apex wins because TopstepX restricts third-party platforms."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Apex vs MyFundedFutures (MFFU) — which is cheaper?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU's Core plan is generally cheaper than Apex's eval at the same account size, especially because MFFU eliminated activation fees entirely in July 2025. Apex 4.0 eval + activation fee combined sometimes exceeds MFFU's all-in cost. Both allow automation; MFFU is more permissive on copy trading."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Apex vs Tradeify — quality comparison?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Tradeify 3.0 (March 2026) eliminated subscriptions like Apex 4.0 did. Tradeify's Lightning plan offers instant funding which Apex doesn't. Tradeify allows news trading freely; Apex 4.0 also allows it. Apex has bigger search volume and longer track record; Tradeify has won \"Most User Friendly\" prop firm awards. Both are reasonable choices."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Did Topstep also halt metals like Apex did?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Topstep restricted some metals contracts in early 2026, similar industry response to volatility. Specifics vary; check Topstep's permitted products list for current state."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I run Apex on Mac?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Tradovate has a native Mac client. NinjaTrader requires Parallels or a VM on Mac. Most Mac users go with Tradovate web or the Tradovate desktop app for Apex."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the Apex Discord — is it official?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex maintains an official Discord community accessible from the support site. Active community discussions, payout announcements, rule clarifications. Always verify \"official Apex\" Discord links from apextraderfunding.com — fake Apex Discords exist for phishing."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I set trading time restrictions or pause trading around news events for my Apex account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections. You can configure specific active trading windows with start and end times (24-hour ET format). Any TradingView alerts received outside your configured hours are automatically rejected — no new trades are placed. Existing open positions remain active. Settings can be applied to specific accounts or all accounts at once. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/ For Tradovate connections, PickMyTrade also integrates with ForexFactory to automatically pause trading before and after scheduled news events — it can close open positions and cancel pending limit/stop orders during news windows. Tradovate Trading Time guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.trade/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use a bot or automated strategy on an Apex evaluation or PA?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Apex Trader Funding's Prohibited Activities page says \"No Automation or Algorithm Usage allowed\" and explains that rewards are meant for human traders, \"not to reward automated systems executing preprogrammed logic.\" The page makes no exception for evaluations or Performance Accounts (PAs), so read it as covering both. Apex refers traders to its user agreement for the full wording and invites questions through its help desk. If any tool would place orders for you from preset signals, get Apex's answer in writing before connecting it to an Apex account."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I copy trade across my own Apex PA accounts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, within limits. Apex says \"Copy trading across PA accounts under your personal name and business name is allowed,\" but the hedging rule still applies and all PAs must trade in the same direction. The cap is 20 active PAs across everyone in your household, your companies and connections, on Rithmic, Tradovate or WealthCharts. Going over 20 makes you ineligible for payout and can bring forfeiture, closure of all PAs and a permanent ban. Copying with other people is different: Apex's Prohibited Activities page lists sharing \"trade copying with other traders\" as strictly forbidden."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is long NQ and short MNQ hedging at Apex, even if the positions are on different accounts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Apex's Prohibited Activities page bans \"holding both long and short positions simultaneously on the same or correlated instrument,\" so long NQ against short MNQ counts. For PAs, its copy-trading rule says accounts must \"not hedge against correlated assets,\" and for evaluations Apex says you \"may not pass Evaluation Accounts by hedging them against each other.\" Apex does not publish a list of correlated instruments, so treat products that usually move together as correlated. On an EOD PA, hedging violations \"will result in immediate account closure.\""
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use a VPN or VPS with Apex Trader Funding?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Apex's rule targets the purpose, not the tool. Its Prohibited Activities page bans VPNs, proxy servers, cloud servers and anonymizing tools when used \"for the purpose of misrepresenting, concealing, or disguising your identity, device, or location\" to evade rules, hide violations or commit fraud. The same page forbids sharing \"MAC addresses, computers, IPs\" with other traders. A VPS does not change the separate automation ban: running an automated strategy on a cloud server is still prohibited at Apex."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does Apex's EOD drawdown work, and can my balance dip below it during the day?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No, it cannot dip below it. Apex recalculates the EOD threshold once per trading day at 4:59:59 PM ET from your closing balance, and it only moves up. It is \"enforced in real time\": if your balance touches or falls below it at any moment, positions are liquidated and the evaluation fails or the PA closes. On a 50K account with $2,000 drawdown, a $50,800 close moves the threshold to $48,800. On PAs it stops trailing at starting balance plus $100. Intraday trailing accounts differ: that threshold trails the highest intraday balance."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do I have to close my trades before the market closes at Apex?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Apex's trading times page says \"All trades must be closed before 4:59 PM ET,\" and it is your responsibility to be flat by then. Agricultural futures close earlier (2:05 PM ET for livestock, 2:20 PM ET for grains), and holiday sessions can close early. Holding positions through the close is on Apex's prohibited list, and traders who do it \"will forfeit their accounts and all associated balances.\" A new trading day starts at 6:00 PM ET."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What do I need to request a payout on an Apex PA, and does a consistency rule apply?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "On EOD and Intraday PAs, Apex requires at least 5 trading days that each meet a minimum daily profit (for example $250 on a 50K EOD PA, $200 on a 50K Intraday PA), a $500 minimum payout, and a balance above the Safety Net, which is the drawdown limit plus $100. A 50% consistency rule applies: no single profitable day may be 50% or more of profit since your last approved payout. Each PA can receive at most six payouts, each with a cap, paid at a 100% split. Legacy accounts have their own rules."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How many contracts can I trade on Apex, and how many PAs can I hold?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on account size and stage. Apex EOD Evaluations allow 4, 6, 8 and 12 max contracts on the 25K, 50K, 100K and 150K sizes. EOD PAs allow 2, 4, 6 and 10, with tier-based scaling, so position size grows as your end-of-day balance moves up scaling levels. Apex lists \"breaching the maximum allowed contracts per an account plan\" as prohibited manipulation. You may hold up to 20 active PAs combined, and \"There are no limits to Evaluation accounts.\""
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade during news like CPI or FOMC at Apex?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, with your normal strategy. Apex's Prohibited Activities page says \"Trading during news is allowed for your normal trading strategy.\" What it bans are news strategies that \"chase the market\" or place orders on both sides to gamble on the outcome. Its manipulation rule also names \"non-directional bracket trading, where orders are left open on both sides of the market.\" Holding a long and a short at the same time during a news spike also breaks the hedging ban."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
